		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=146&amp;p=1340#p1340"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hi,<br><blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Well, it took me 8 hours to install mono-complete on a RPi 3 A+ <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":-D" title="Very Happy"><br><br>Replace the udev rules file with the attached one, then execute the following (or reboot):<br><br><strong class="text-strong">sudo udevadm control --reload-rules</strong><br><br>Cheers.</div></blockquote>Yikes. 8 hours is a long time. Possibly a faster MicroSD would work better. I'm sure it didn't take me that long.<br><br>I tried the rules file you sent, and it didn't work either, but this time I found where the logs went.<br><div class="codebox"><p>CODE: </p><pre><code>Dec 01 19:30:26 pi systemd-udevd[12613]: Process '/bin/bash -c 'ID=$(echo /devices/platform/soc/3f980000.usb/usb1/1-1/1-1.4/1-1.4:1.0/usbmisc/hiddev0 | cut -d/ -f8); echo $ID &gt; /sys/bus/usb/drivers/usbhid/unbind'' failed with exit code 1.</code></pre></div>Looking at what's going on there, I wonder if grabbing the third in from the end would work better than grabbing the 7th or 8th depending on platform. You can do this using cut by using rev before and after. The following rule worked for me. If it works on non-Rasbian installations that would be great. I don't know what $devpath is on other Linuxes, but you may.<br><div class="codebox"><p>CODE: </p><pre><code>KERNEL=="hiddev*", ATTRS{idVendor}=="15a2", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0073", MODE="0666", GROUP="plugdev", RUN+="/bin/bash -c 'ID=$(echo %p | rev | cut -d/ -f3 | rev); echo $ID &gt; /sys/bus/usb/drivers/usbhid/unbind'"</code></pre></div>I also tried to find a better way, but I haven't found it yet.</div></blockquote>Okay. I guess you're using a RPi 4, beast I don't own. Yep, reversing should work regardless platforms.<br><br>So, are you able to flash your GD now ?<br><br>Cheers.<br>---<br>Daniel</div></blockquote>Try with this line as replacement:<br><div class="codebox"><p>CODE: </p><pre><code>KERNEL=="hiddev*", ATTRS{idVendor}=="15a2", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0073", MODE="0666", GROUP="plugdev", RUN+="/bin/bash -c 'ID=$(IFS=/; read -a array &lt;&lt;&lt; %p; echo ${array[-3]}); echo $ID &gt; /sys/bus/usb/drivers/usbhid/unbind'"</code></pre></div><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Mon Dec 02, 2019 5:44 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
